From 53661d8f129b13e59191b51d6ae2ebf9ef8b3505 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Xun2202 <xun2202@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 06:14:42 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] android: ask for battery optimisation exemption and hold a
 wake lock while caching
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

A dataSync foreground service got the notification shown on HarmonyOS
卓易通, but a lock-screen screenshot two minutes after backgrounding
shows the notification frozen at its last value while FlClash's keeps
updating: the process was still suspended. FlClash requests
REQUEST_IGNORE_BATTERY_OPTIMIZATIONS; do the same from
HttpCacheServiceController the first time a download starts while the
app is in the foreground (never again once granted), and hold a partial
wake lock for the lifetime of HttpCacheService. This build is not
distributed through Play, so the policy lint (BatteryLife) does not apply.
